      "desc": "Upload a video, adjust FPS and width, and convert it to an animated GIF in one click.",
      "guide": {
        "steps": [
          "Click \"Upload video\" and choose MP4 / MOV / WebM.",
          "Drag the timeline to set start/end, and pick frame rate and size (e.g. 10fps, 480px wide).",
          "Click \"Generate GIF\". The browser encodes locally and downloads the animation."
        ],
        "explanationTitle": "Key points for video to GIF",
        "formula": "GIF frames ≈ duration × frame rate; smaller size and lower fps mean a lighter file",
        "explanation": [
          "GIF is a widely supported looping format, great for memes, tutorial clips, or social posts. Since GIF has no efficient compression, keep clips short (a few seconds) and lower the frame rate and resolution to avoid huge files.",
          "Trimming and encoding run locally with no upload, so you can quickly turn highlights into shareable animations."
        ],
        "faq": [
          {
            "q": "The GIF is too big?",
            "a": "Shorten the clip, lower the frame rate (10–15fps), or reduce width to shrink it noticeably."
          },
          {
            "q": "How long a video?",
            "a": "A few seconds is best; very long clips make oversized GIFs that load slowly."
          },
          {
            "q": "Is my video uploaded?",
            "a": "No. All trimming and encoding happen locally in your browser."
          }
        ]
      }
