          "If the video has to be inserted into a fixed upload or storage budget, it can be extrapolated from size to size.",
          "Leave a margin for the cost of the containment and audio; the calculator will first remove the audio and the video will receive the remainder.",
          "Bitrate is the number of data per second of video, which directly determines the quality and volume of the painting. ** Code and resolution must match**: the same 8 Mbps to 1080p is clear, and 4K is a piece (because the pixel number is four times the pixel number, the data distributed to each pixel is only 1/4. Empirical law: 1080p about 8 Mbps, 4K about 35-45 Mbps is the starting point for \"sufficient\" and high dynamic content (sport events, video games) requires a higher number.",
          "**The three control modes for the **code rate**: CBR (fixed rate, required for live broadcasting, of a predictable size but with the least painting efficiency), VBR (variable rate, recorded recommendation, complex scene automatic coding rate, best homogeneity) and CRF (consistent mass, x 264/x265 commonly used, you specify quality target 0-51, automatic codifier decision rate, ** CRF mode is most economical ** - values are lower in quality, 18 are near non-destructive, 23 are commonly used without loss of sight, 28 documents are significantly smaller but can see compression marks)."
