            "a": "It's inevitable — all platforms are coded. What can be done is ** to feed the Platform to the highest quality of the source**: 1 upload at the upper limit of the Platform ' s recommended code rate (reserved for secondary compression); 2 using the Platform ' s preferred encoders and parameters (Youtube recommends H264 + high-code rate MP4); 3 resolution to keep the original (do not sample); and 4 to avoid material that has already been pressed many times. In addition, the platform allocates better coding resources to high-visibility videos (VP9/AV1 for YouTube) which is a long-term benefit."
