          "Practical techniques: A rough estimate of 22/7 ≈ 3.1429 is sufficient (about 0.04% error) when the numeric number cannot be remembered, or 355/13 ≈ 3.1415929, which is the exact score after the decimal six, which was found by the ancient mathematicians' ancestors. The project estimate was 3.14, with a 0.05 per cent error and no impact on most scenarios."
