        "explanationTitle": "Comparing hypervisors",
        "formula": "score = w1×features + w2×(1/cost) + w3×support; pick max(score)",
        "explanation": [
          "Hypervisors differ in licensing model (free, per-core, subscription), ecosystem maturity and management tooling, not just raw performance.",
          "The cheapest option can become the most expensive if it lacks the automation, backup or support your team depends on daily."
        ],
        "faq": [
          {
            "q": "Is free hypervisor good enough?",
            "a": "For labs yes, but production usually needs support, live migration and backup APIs that free tiers omit."
          },
          {
            "q": "What matters most for selection?",
            "a": "Match feature depth to your actual ops: backups, HA, and management tooling often beat raw speed."
